<article class="env-lemma" id="08ZJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08ZJ">Lemma <span data-tag="08ZJ">5.5.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a set. Given any collection $\mathcal{B}$ of subsets of $X$ there is a unique topology on $X$ such that $\mathcal{B}$ is a subbase for this topology. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By convention $\bigcap _\emptyset B = X $. Thus we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0D5P" data-tag="0D5P">5.5.2</a> to the set of finite intersections of elements from $\mathcal B$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>